Task 2.1 Basic Terminal Operations
Current-directory display (pwd) | [Shows the full path of the folder you are currently inside]
| Directory listing (ls) [Lists the names of files and folders in your current location] 
| Detailed listing (ls -l) [Lists files and folders with extra details like permissions, size, and date modified.] 
| Change directory (cd) | [Moves you one level up to the parent folder]
| Create directory (mkdir) | [Creates a new empty folder] 
| Create empty file (touch) | [Creates a new empty file] 
| Copy file (cp) | [Makes a duplicate of a file with a new name or location] 
| Move / rename file (mv) | [Renames a file or moves it to another folder without leaving a duplicate] 
| Display file contents (cat) | [Prints the text inside a file directly onto the Terminal screen] 

