Task 4 - My Understanding

Through this mission, I learned how to navigate folders and manage files directly using text commands in the Terminal instead of relying on a graphical file manager. Using commands like pwd, ls, mkdir, touch, cp, and mv made it clear how fast and precise file operations become once you know your current directory path. I also understood that flags modify how commands behave (such as showing hidden files or detailed sizes), pipes (|) connect commands together by passing the output of one into another, and package managers automate installing and updating software safely from the command line.
